      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm experiencing the same problem.\n\nIn attached video, using TweenLocalRotation to animate a lever. \n\nAs you can see, it moves, but the rotation doesn't follow the correct axis.\n\nCurrently, VRCTween doesn't seem to provide a way to lock/fix the rotation axis, which is causing this issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-23T14:19:26.824Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In comparison to DOTween's corresponding methods, VRCTween.Tween(Local)Rotation and Tween(Local)Path skips RotateMode/PathMode parameters.\n\nWith original DOTween we can tweak subtle behavior of rotation amount and look-at direction respectively.\n\nCurrent VRCTween does not have them so we have to use Virtual Tweens to interpolate in that way (e.g. rotate Transform beyond 360°).\n\nAre they intentionally omitted? If so, what is the reason for that, for performance or API complexity?\n\nIt may make VRCTween more attractive to export these types and take as parameters (in last position).",
